21. Example Backend APIs
POST /api/routes
GET /api/weather
GET /api/traffic
GET /api/incidents
GET /api/hazards
POST /api/report
POST /api/reroute
GET /api/safe-zones
Example route request:
{
  "origin": "Salem",
  "destination": "Attur",
  "mode": "bike",
  "priority": "safety"
}
The response can contain the recommended route, distance, ETA and risk level.
22. Database Design
Users:
user_id, name, preferences, vehicle_type
Incidents:
incident_id, type, latitude, longitude, severity, timestamp, status
Routes:
route_id, origin, destination, distance, time, risk_score
Historical Data:
timestamp, location, traffic, weather, accidents, flood, risk
Possible databases include Firebase, MongoDB or PostgreSQL.
23. Technology Stack
Frontend: HTML/CSS/JavaScript or React
Mapping: Google Maps or Mapbox
Backend: Node.js
Framework: Express.js
Language: TypeScript
Database: Firebase / MongoDB / PostgreSQL
Machine Learning: Python + Scikit-learn
Data Processing: Pandas + NumPy
APIs: Maps, Traffic, Weather and Incident sources
Deployment: Vercel / Render / Railway
Version Control: Git + GitHub
