25. Recommended Development Phases
Phase 1 – Basic Map:
Build the map, origin, destination and basic route display.
Phase 2 – Multiple Routes:
Display and compare alternative routes.
Phase 3 – Real-Time Data:
Integrate traffic, weather and incident information.
Phase 4 – Risk Engine:
Create a rule-based risk scoring system.
Phase 5 – Machine Learning:
Train and integrate a Random Forest risk prediction model.
Phase 6 – Route Optimization:
Combine safety, distance and travel time.
Phase 7 – Dynamic Rerouting:
Monitor the route and reroute when risk changes.
Phase 8 – User Reports:
Add community-based incident reporting.
Phase 9 – Deployment:
Deploy frontend, backend, database and ML service.
26. What Makes Route 360 Different?
Traditional navigation generally focuses on shortest or fastest routes.
Route 360 combines:
• Distance
• Travel time
• Traffic
• Weather
• Accidents
• Floods
• Road conditions
• User preference
• Machine-learning risk prediction
The result is a safety-aware and dynamically adaptive route recommendation system.
27. SIH Presentation Flow
1. Problem – Fastest route does not always mean safest route.
2. Solution – Route 360 provides safety-aware route recommendations.
3. Data – Traffic, weather, incidents and historical information.
4. AI – ML predicts road/route risk.
5. Optimization – Safety, time and distance are combined.
6. Demo – Enter destination, compare routes, detect hazard and reroute.
7. Impact – Safer travel, better hazard awareness and improved emergency mobility.
28. Final Project Definition
Route 360 is an intelligent safe-route planning system that collects real-time and historical information about roads, traffic, weather and hazards, predicts road-level risk using machine learning, evaluates alternative routes using safety, travel time and distance, and continuously recommends the most suitable route to the user.
The central idea is simple:
Traditional Navigation:
Shortest / Fastest Route
Route 360:
Safe + Optimal + Adaptive Route